{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nThe board only refreshes on `r` or when the page is re-entered after five minutes. Agents move items across Status columns and edit fields while the page sits open, and those edits are invisible to the GitHub page's change check: measured on the demo project, editing item dates bumped every item's `updatedAt` and **`ProjectV2.updatedAt`** but left the issues' own `updatedAt` untouched.\n\n## Spec\n\n1. **Change detection (1 point)** — while the Projects page is shown, poll `projectV2 { updatedAt }` (measured cost: 1 point) every `projects-poll-interval` and refetch the board (~3 points over the GraphQL path) only when it moved. `Board` carries `updated_at`, read for free by the meta query (fields + views + count), so the first comparison needs no extra request.\n2. **Interval** — a new top-level `projects-poll-interval` (default `\"30s\"`, minimum `\"5s\"`; documented in the Config Reference and defaults dump), separate from the GitHub page's 5 s because each probe costs a point: 120 points/hour with the page open, 20 in idle mode.\n3. **Governed like every other poll** — the #168 refresh scale (idle ×6, under 20 % ×2, stopped under 5 % or with `github-auto-refresh \"off\"`) applies; a rate-limited probe engages the same backoff as the GitHub page.\n4. **Selection survives** — `set_board` already keeps the selected item by id and the shown view; lanes, columns, table sort and roadmap scroll are preserved across the swap.\n5. **Status bar** — the existing `board Ns ago` plus a brief `↻ updated` when a refresh was triggered.\n6. **Fixtures / tests** — the probe joins `vig fixtures record`; unit tests cover unchanged / changed `updatedAt`; the fixture integration test checks that an unchanged probe does not refetch.\n\nCompanion of the GitHub lists issue: that page's REST ETag check is free but blind to project field edits, hence the separate mechanism here.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-09T07:13:44Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":178,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Projects: auto-refresh the board on ProjectV2.updatedAt"}
